KLID, Ⅳ. klidya, P. become wet: 🞄pp. klin-na, wet;
 pr. pt. klindat, wet, 🞄dripping;
 compassionate;
 cs. kledaya, make 🞄wet, moisten;
 dirty, soil. pari, pra = simple 🞄verb. sam, pp. moistened, softened.

KLIŚ, Ⅸ. kliśnā, Ⅳ. kliśya, P. 🞄torment, plague, annoy, trouble;
 Ⅳ. 🞄Ā. (P.) be troubled, tormented, or distressed;
 🞄P. cause pain to (ac.): pp. kliṣṭa, tormented, 🞄annoyed, afflicted;
 damaged, worn 🞄[] 🞄out;
 painful, distressing;
 forced, obscure;
 cs. 🞄kleśaya = simple vb. pari, Ⅳ. P. Ā. suffer 🞄distress: pp. tormented, distressed, afflicted;
 🞄weakly: -m, ad. reluctantly;
 cs. torment. 🞄saṃ-pra, knead, squeeze.

klībá, a. emasculated, impotent;
 unmanly, 🞄timorous, cowardly;
 waterless (cloud);
 🞄m. eunuch;
 weakling, coward;
 n. neuter 🞄(gender): -tā, f. impotency;
 weakness.
